---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import NavBar from "../components/NavBar.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Reliability Guide | ContentFlow App"
  description="Practical notes on auth and resilience behavior in ContentFlow App."
>
  <main class="page-shell">
    <NavBar />

    <section class="section">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Resilience Notes</p>
        <h1 class="page-title">Reliable authentication and degraded workflows.</h1>
        <p>
          This site keeps a practical model for operational behavior: auth entrypoints,
          session continuity, and offline continuity paths are documented separately
          from full external publishing channels.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="pricing-grid">
        <article class="price-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Auth entrypoints</p>
          <h2>Web auth is the active production path</h2>
          <p>
            The app uses Clerk-based sign-in/sign-up and SSO callback paths for
            session bootstrap, with explicit startup checks before entering the
            main shell.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="price-card accent-card">
          <p class="eyebrow">Operational expectation</p>
          <h2>Do not collapse auth and publish flow</h2>
          <p>
            The shell handles onboarding and workflow orchestration; external channel
            publish coverage is intentionally marked as explicitly partial where
            not yet fully closed.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <div class="doc-grid">
        <article class="doc-card">
          <h3>Queue behavior</h3>
          <p>
            Supported write actions are queued when sync is not available and replayed
            when the connection is restored.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="doc-card">
          <h3>Recovery visibility</h3>
          <p>
            Recovery states are not hidden. Operators can see what is pending and when
            it is being reconciled.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="doc-card">
          <h3>Non-goals</h3>
          <p>
            Some publish-adjacent loops remain in-progress and are tracked in specs
            rather than hidden as completed.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
